{
  "info": {
    "name": "💬 Message Service - E2EE & Server-Side Chat",
    "description": "🔐 **DUAL ENCRYPTION ARCHITECTURE**\n\n**✅ FEATURES:**\n- 🔒 **E2EE Private Chats** (Admin cannot read - RSA-2048 + AES-256)\n- 💬 **Server-Side Chats** (Admin can read - Marketplace/Support/Dispute)\n- 🔑 **Key Management** (Public key registration & retrieval)\n- 👮 **Admin Tools** (Monitor server-side chats, flag, search)\n- ⚡ **Real-time** WebSocket + REST API\n- 📱 **Multi-device** sync & offline messages\n\n**📊 CHAT TYPES:**\n- `private`: E2EE encrypted, zero-knowledge, admin blocked\n- `marketplace`: Server-side, admin readable, dispute resolution\n- `support`: Server-side, customer service, ticket assignment\n- `dispute`: Server-side, evidence preservation, priority handling\n\n**🔧 ARCHITECTURE:**\n```\nE2EE Flow:\n1. Client generates RSA keypair\n2. Upload public key to server\n3. Retrieve recipient's public key\n4. Encrypt message with AES-256\n5. Encrypt AES key with recipient's RSA public key\n6. Server stores encrypted data (cannot decrypt)\n\nServer-Side Flow:\n1. Client sends plaintext message\n2. Server stores plaintext\n3. Admin can view/search/flag for moderation\n```\n\n**🎯 SERVICE INFO:**\n- Port: 4008 (HTTP + WebSocket)\n- WebSocket: ws://localhost:4008 (Socket.IO)\n- Auth: JWT Bearer token\n- Database: MongoDB (viepropchain)\n\n**📖 DOCUMENTATION:**\nSee E2EE_ARCHITECTURE.md for complete implementation guide\n\n**🚀 QUICK TEST:**\n1. Login & get JWT token\n2. Register E2EE keys (Key Management)\n3. Send E2EE private message\n4. Send server-side marketplace message\n5. Admin view server-side (blocks E2EE)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔑 Key Management (E2EE)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Public Key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    console.log(\"✅ Public key registered\");",
                  "    console.log(\"🔑 Fingerprint: \" + jsonData.data.key_fingerprint);",
                  "    console.log(\"📱 Device: \" + jsonData.data.device_name);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{jwt_token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"public_key\": \"-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\\nMIIBIjANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQEFAAOCAQ8AMIIBCgKCAQEA1234...\\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\",\n  \"device_name\": \"Chrome on Windows\",\n  \"platform\": \"web\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:4008/api/messages/keys/register",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["localhost"],
              "port": "4008",
              "path": ["api", "messages", "keys", "register"]
            },
            "description": "🔑 **Register User's Public Key for E2EE**\n\n**Purpose:** Store user's RSA public key for E2EE encryption\n\n**Client-side Key Generation (Web Crypto API):**\n```javascript\nconst keyPair = await window.crypto.subtle.generateKey(\n  { name: \"RSA-OAEP\", modulusLength: 2048, publicExponent: new Uint8Array([1, 0, 1]), hash: \"SHA-256\" },\n  true,\n  [\"encrypt\", \"decrypt\"]\n);\n\nconst publicKey = await window.crypto.subtle.exportKey(\"spki\", keyPair.publicKey);\nconst publicKeyPem = arrayBufferToBase64(publicKey);\n// Store privateKey in IndexedDB securely\n```\n\n**Body:**\n- `public_key`: PEM-formatted RSA public key (2048-bit)\n- `device_name`: Human-readable device identifier\n- `platform`: \"web\", \"ios\", \"android\"\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Public key registered successfully\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"user_id\": \"user123\",\n    \"key_fingerprint\": \"abc123...\",\n    \"device_name\": \"Chrome on Windows\",\n    \"active\": true\n  }\n}\n```"
          }
        },
